From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:14:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] i386-asm: the "X" constraint on i386, constants printed in
 the width of their type

The "X" constraint (any operand) was accepted on x86_64 only; gcc takes
it everywhere.  A constant "i" operand printed as its 64-bit value, gcc
prints it sign-extended in the width of its type: "i"(0x80000000u) is
$-2147483648 (so "movq %1, %0" sign-extends as it does with gcc),
"i"((unsigned char)200) is $-56, a _Bool is 0 or 1.

Fix 100 of the tinycc-os-kernel project (docs/FIX-LOG.md).
---
 i386-asm.c | 15 ++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/i386-asm.c b/i386-asm.c
index 0e2989d..23b7c6f 100644
--- a/i386-asm.c
+++ b/i386-asm.c
@@ -1618,10 +1618,10 @@ static inline int constraint_priority(const char *str)
         case 'x':
             pr = 3;
             break;
+#endif
         case 'X':
             pr = 4;
             break;
-#endif
         case '@':
             /* "=@cc<cond>" flag output: needs a general register */
             return 3;
@@ -2122,6 +2122,19 @@ ST_FUNC void subst_asm_operand(CString *add_str,
            runtime_const_ptr() places `mov $0x0123456789abcdef, %reg`
            and patches the 8 immediate bytes later */
         val = sv->c.i;
+        if (!(r & VT_SYM)) {
+            /* like gcc, in the width of the operand's type and signed:
+               "i"(0x80000000u) is $-2147483648, "i"((unsigned char)200) $-56 */
+            int bt = sv->type.t & VT_BTYPE;
+            if (bt == VT_INT)
+                val = (int32_t)val;
+            else if (bt == VT_SHORT)
+                val = (int16_t)val;
+            else if (bt == VT_BYTE)
+                val = (int8_t)val;
+            else if (bt == VT_BOOL)
+                val = val != 0;
+        }
         if (modifier == 'n')
             val = -val;
         cstr_printf(add_str, "%lld", val);
